:: reading.painting1.evening
{=

It is dark outside, but your mind is alight. You close your eyes and ($funcReveal: "see...", "see")

|see)[(either:
    [` `the Sun's ($funcReveal: "twin sister", "openedEyes") - red, rippling, and roiling beneath the surface of an obsidian lake.],
    [` `a red ($funcReveal: "slit", "openedEyes") in space, where the air peels to reveal what lies dreaming behind all things.],
    [` `violet ($funcReveal: "rays", "openedEyes") pulsating across the blackness of your lids, tracing the path with which the stars hurl through the void.],
)]

|see)[
<br>
There it is. In the light of night, all the hidden creatures have come out to play.
]

|openedEyes)[
<br>
But with open eyes, reality yet falls short. Here, the canvas depicts only your failure - thus far - to render this vision in oil.
<br>
($funcReveal: "What else is there to do but paint?", "work")

]

|work)[
<br>
Your Work has always been performed when the world sleeps. No-one will see. No-one will know. No sneer nor praise.
<br>
$cssDesc[No time like now.]

(t8n: "dissolve")(show:?mainDone)
]

:: done.painting1.evening [unfinished]
